On 21 July 2010 22:13, Luke Bergen <lukeabergen@gmail.com> wrote:

> I would hope that the lad would be male... a female lad would be a
> confusing thing.


Many characters from the kids shows/animations I know have a-sexual or
ambivalent traits. Particularly the Japanese animes, which can often
strikingly differ from the 'gender-amplified' American cartoons. You can
tell it from for instance the fact that many male characters (children or
adults) in animes are voiced by female actresses in the original Japanese
versions, while they are voiced by 'tough' male actors in the American
versions. Dragon Ball Z is a good example: Goku (an adult male fighter) is
voiced by a female; Gohan (Goku's son) is also voiced by a female; Kuririn
(Goku's friend and male fighter) is also voiced by a female; Freeza (one of
the strongest villains) is voiced by a male but has no physical
characteristics of either male or female while relatively anthropomorphic.
In another very famous and influencial Japanese manga called JoJo's Bizarre
Adventure, many supposedly male characters have somewhat female looks (while
the author is a married male heterosexual):
http://www.onemanga.com/Jojo's_Bizarre_Adventure/470/01/<http://www.onemanga.com/Jojo%27s_Bizarre_Adventure/470/01/>

